From: R. Matthew Emerson <rme@acm.org>
Subject: [PATCH] TEST ONLY: sled the post-fix unbind_interrupt_level window (32-bit ARM)

Test instrumentation for the unbind_interrupt_level missed-suspend
reproducer, POST-FIX form, 32-bit ARM.  Holds open the corresponding
window in the fixed code, between the *INTERRUPT-LEVEL* restore and the
flags poll: a suspend signal that lands here sees the restored level,
parks normally, and must NOT be missed.  The same delay at the
corresponding point makes the pre/post comparison fair.

Contributed by the maintainer on the pull request that adds this
directory, with the measurement: 2000 of 2000 world stops, no misses.

Applies to the tree WITH the 32-bit ARM fix.  Mutually exclusive with
the pre-fix sled.  NEVER MERGE.
---

diff --git a/lisp-kernel/arm-spentry.s b/lisp-kernel/arm-spentry.s
index b6bde1e..0c64e4d 100644
--- a/lisp-kernel/arm-spentry.s
+++ b/lisp-kernel/arm-spentry.s
@@ -2690,6 +2690,12 @@ _spentry(unbind_interrupt_level)
         __(ldr imm0,[imm0,#binding.link])
         __(str temp1,[temp2,#INTERRUPT_LEVEL_BINDING_INDEX])   /* restore first */
         __(str imm0,[rcontext,#tcr.db_link])
+        /* TEST ONLY, NEVER MERGE: hold the post-fix window (restore ->
+           flags poll) open, the same delay as the prefix sled so the
+           pre/post comparison is fair.  imm1 is dead here. */
+        __(mov imm1,#0x400000)
+9:      __(subs imm1,imm1,#1)
+        __(bne 9b)
         __(cmp temp1,#-2<<fixnumshift)
         __(ble 1f)                      /* restored level still defers */
         __(ldr imm0,[rcontext,#tcr.flags])                     /* poll after restore */
